  I think you're on to something there.  Conducts can make 
Nethack nearly impossible.  If that's not enough, then players 
aren't really interested in a more difficult Nethack.

  So it doesn't seem so much that players think Nethack is too 
easy.  It's more that they don't think Nethack is interesting 
enough.


  Gehennom gets mentioned a lot in this context.  Players think
its too long and boring.  They want a more interesting challenge
instead.

  Yet I now realize that's why Gehennom is the way it is.  No one
gets a free ride through it on the Ascension Run.  Every 
ascension, first time or thirtieth time, has to slog up through 
Gehennom.  There are ways to alleviate the pain, but no way to 
avoid it completely.

  Ditto with the Elemental Planes.

  To a (mere ;^) mortal Gehennom is endlessly terrifying, but not
boring.  To the regular ascender, it's endlessly boring.  So much
so that some players will start a new game rather than go through
it again.


  And that's the way it should be.  Ascension should not be the
natural outcome of most Nethack games.  An ascension should also 
mean more than that the player has skill in Nethack.  It should 
mean the player spent a lot of time/effort in that game.

  And it does.


